    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **48 run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp35Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match (possible-duplicate) rule for owner creation. When a new owner clears the hard-duplicate identity check but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a different telephone, it is still created, flagged `possibleDuplicate: true`, with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These generate onto `OwnerDto` and are auto-mapped by MapStruct.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` columns with getters/setters (mirroring the existing derived fields like `bulkSignupWarning`).\n- **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table. (Tests run on HSQLDB.)\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the hard-duplicate identity check, computes the soft match via a new `findPossibleDuplicate(lastName, postcode, normalizedTelephone)` helper and stamps the flag/id onto the owner before saving.\n\nMatch semantics in the helper: `lastName` compared case-insensitively, `postcode` compared exactly (both required non-blank, since a shared postcode is needed to match), normalized telephone must differ, and when multiple owners match the earliest (lowest id) is chosen for deterministic results.",
